  "Question": "What is \\(C(5,1)+C(5,2)\\)?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "15",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(5+10=15\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Combine adjacent coefficients\n\nThe lower indices are consecutive, so Pascal's identity combines the two coefficients. For integers \\(1\\le k\\le n\\), it states \\(C(n,k-1)+C(n,k)=C(n+1,k)\\). Taking \\(n=5\\) and \\(k=2\\) gives\n\\[\nC(5,1)+C(5,2)=C(6,2)=\\frac{6\\cdot5}{2\\cdot1}=15.\n\\]\nThus the value is \\(15\\).",
